# gen_fu_warl_res_backstop: the WARL generator asserted on its own draw at 4 of 301 seeds

WHAT THIS CLAIMS. gen_pmp_csr_warl_prog.py can draw a TP-PMP-003 phase in which no write
presents reserved pmpcfg bits, and its own assertion then refuses to produce a program. The
backstop adds one directed set-type write in exactly that case. Claimed here: the assertion
reproduces, the backstop removes it, and no other seed's program changes. NOT claimed: any
simulation result; the fix rides the generator group's sweep for that.

THE MECHANISM, from the committed source. tp003 draws 4 to 8 writes and marks one as a
reserved-bit write when the COMBINED value carries bits 6:5 in some lane. A clear-type write
cannot: combined() returns old & ~operand for csrrc, and this implementation stores no
reserved pmpcfg field (ibex_pkg pmp_cfg_t carries lock, mode, exec, write and read only), so
the read-back has bits 6:5 zero and the AND-NOT keeps them zero. A phase whose every draw
picks csrrc therefore has no qualifying write, and the assertion at the end of tp003 fires.
With one form of three drawn per write and 4 to 8 writes, that is about one seed in fifty.

THE FIX draws only when the loop produced none, which is what keeps every other seed's
program byte-identical: it is placed before the assertion, inside tp003, so it covers both
phases; it picks the first entry group the phase already judged writable, sets bits 6:5 in
its lanes with a csrrs, and records the op the same way the loop does.

INPUTS BY DIGEST (sha256 first 12).
  generator at HEAD, the subject of the red                7f062657722d
  generator with the backstop (working tree, uncommitted)  964e232edfb4

THE SWEEP: 301 seeds, runtime-2's failing seed 230969025 first, then 300 consecutive seeds
from the block's own base seed 218090305. Both generators are loaded as modules side by side
and each seed's emitted text is hashed, so a difference is a difference in the PROGRAM, not
in a rendering. An earlier run of this same comparison was INVALID and is named here rather
than dropped: a copy loop overwrote the extracted HEAD generator with the working-tree one,
so both sides were the fixed generator and the sweep reported no assertion at all. The
digests above are printed by the sweep for that reason.

RESULT. 4 of 301 seeds assert at HEAD and none with the backstop; the 297 seeds that build
at HEAD produce byte-identical programs either way. Both phases appear among the four, which
is why the backstop sits inside tp003 rather than at one call site.

